<div class="container">
  <div class="page-label">Legal</div>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: May 11, 2026</p>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p><strong>Short version:</strong> We collect your email and subscription status to run your account. We never log your VPN traffic, browsing activity, or connection metadata. We don't sell your data. Ever.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
  <p>RedGuard ("we", "us", "our") is an endpoint security product providing antivirus and VPN services for Windows. Our website is redgaurd.com. For privacy questions, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@redgaurd.com">privacy@redgaurd.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. What We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect only what we need to provide the service:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> Your email address and a hashed password when you register.</li>
    <li><strong>Subscription status:</strong> Your plan tier (Free, Pro, Enterprise) and billing status, received via Shopify when you purchase.</li>
    <li><strong>Scan metadata:</strong> File hashes, scan results, and threat verdicts for files you submit. We do not store the contents of your files — only their cryptographic hashes and analysis results.</li>
    <li><strong>App telemetry:</strong> App version, OS version, and basic crash reports to improve reliability. No personal data is included.</li>
    <li><strong>Support communications:</strong> If you contact support, we retain those messages to resolve your issue.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What We Do NOT Collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>VPN connection logs, browsing history, DNS queries, or IP addresses while using the VPN.</li>
    <li>The contents of files scanned — only their hashes.</li>
    <li>Location data beyond what is implicit in your IP address at account registration.</li>
    <li>Any data from your device beyond what the RedGuard app explicitly sends.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To authenticate your account and enforce your subscription tier.</li>
    <li>To deliver scan results and threat intelligence.</li>
    <li>To send transactional emails (account confirmation, threat alerts if enabled, billing receipts).</li>
    <li>To improve detection accuracy using aggregated, anonymized scan metadata.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your data for advertising, profiling, or any purpose beyond operating and improving the RedGuard service.</p>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of trusted third parties to operate RedGuard:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Shopify</strong> — processes payments. Shopify's privacy policy governs payment data.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivers transactional emails. Only your email address is shared.</li>
    <li><strong>VirusTotal / AlienVault OTX</strong> — file hashes and extracted IOCs are queried against these threat intelligence platforms. No personal data is shared.</li>
    <li><strong>DigitalOcean</strong> — our infrastructure provider. Data is stored on servers in the United States.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with any third party for marketing purposes.</p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account data is retained while your account is active and for 90 days after deletion.</li>
    <li>Scan history is retained for 12 months and then automatically purged.</li>
    <li>You can request deletion of all your data at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@redgaurd.com">privacy@redgaurd.com</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>All data in transit is encrypted using TLS 1.2 or higher. Passwords are hashed using bcrypt and never stored in plaintext. We conduct periodic security reviews of our infrastructure.</p>

  <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on your location, you may have rights including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access to the personal data we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Correction of inaccurate data.</li>
    <li>Deletion of your account and associated data.</li>
    <li>Portability of your data in a machine-readable format.</li>
    <li>Objection to certain processing.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:privacy@redgaurd.com">privacy@redgaurd.com</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>RedGuard is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will delete it promptly.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. When we do, we'll update the date at the top and notify users by email for material changes. Continued use of RedGuard after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:privacy@redgaurd.com">privacy@redgaurd.com</a></p>
</div>

